  "scope": [
    "Hold scheduling, clocks, expert/weight placement and BF16 rounding fixed. Both cuts consume the original rounded residual with external premix. The producer retains the BF16 store for its later Post reader. Reuse one read for Y and both sides of the BF16 Y handoff to norm. Two-read case also forwards the residual to HcPre cast while retaining the FP32 workspace store/load, Cube Gram, HF32 projection, coefficient outputs and FP32 router plane.",
    "A candidate two-read implementation emits the original BF16 residual and the exact widened activation from Post, plus weighted Y into the norm calculation. The Cube still loads from global memory; replace the old cast writer with this producer. Retarget the Cube address/row stride to a full or tiled wide plane, reserve it through both Cube uses, and preserve all later residual readers. A 25% or 50% writing surcharge charges only that fraction of the original FP32 store-equivalent cost, on every active site, before combining TP and DP. Added synchronization, spills and normalization cost can reduce savings further.",
    "Count 40 FFN entries and only 34 directly adjacent Attention entries. Skip the initialization, auxiliary and Engram cases on the Attention side. Charge separate original tasks, cap each eager stage, apply the TP extrema to the archived EP16 merge, and re-rank eight actual request endpoints. Fixed other work and full downstream exposure. The listed percentages are conditional traffic sensitivities; launch, extra reads, changed kernel duration and stalls can dominate.",
    "Graph estimates use M3 local residual rows per live graph. Ordinary requests use the recorded eager per-rank carrier as HC extent, the original 24-token graph descriptor as M3, and each request’s verification count. Ordinary TTFT includes its own prompt only, excluding other requests and preceding work. No per-request ordinary HC trace was captured. Use both archived response references and a median large-copy rate; small shapes may be launch limited.",
    "FFN paired timing uses nine existing rounds per shape at the same coefficient submission point for both arms. Differences use shared DP skew and the same historical slowest prompt. Matching the round index across independently timed shapes is a transfer scenario, not nine service repetitions. Original post-score work is fixed and coefficient tails fit the recorded slack. The measured producer variant leaves the separate norm and a complete HcPre for coefficients. Its sign does not directly time a fused norm.",
    "In the installed dav_c220 route the standard DataCopy, ND2NZ and padded UB-to-L1 paths stage through GM. No credit for eliminating their two logical global transfers. Cache residence and alternative operand preparation or core mappings remain unknown."
  ],
